{"key": "9782b315bdccc339dba0af134a307d1ab6c20c5414153c47da696ddc8ac117c9", "content": "[{\"file\": \"junit-jupiter-engine/src/main/java/org/junit/jupiter/engine/Constants.java\", \"line\": 211, \"category\": \"design\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"comment\": \"Unlike every other constant in this class, EXTENSIONS_TIMEOUT_THREAD_DUMP_ENABLED_PROPERTY_NAME was updated to delegate to org.junit.jupiter.api.Constants but didn't get the deprecation treatment: no @deprecated Javadoc tag, @API status left as MAINTAINED instead of DEPRECATED, and no @Deprecated(forRemoval = true, since = \\\"6.1\\\") annotation. Looks like this field was missed when the rest of the class was deprecated.\"}]"}
